WEBVTT

00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:04.440
All of us are at least 20 years old!

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:10.440
Clean up your act!

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:13.660
Jeez, you don't have to get so worked up...

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:17.030
<i>Did Nao-san and Makoto-san</i>

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:18.990
<i>get in a fight or something...?</i>

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:59.760
Oh, mornin'. Guess you saw all that then?

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:02.760
Uh, no, I only just woke up...

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:03.810
Yeah?

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:06.930
Sure wouldn't want you to see me at my worst!

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:09.150
I'm assuming that mess right there was the problem?

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:10.100
So you did see it then!

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:15.530
Mornin', Makoto!

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:18.530
I heated up some miso soup with clams
if you want some.

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:20.660
It'll fix up any hangover, I hear!

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:23.200
You have a hangover after a night of drinking alone?

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:24.160
How can you be so dumb?

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:26.910
Don't you go talking to your big sister like that!

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:28.960
Is today recycling day?

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:31.580
No, I just didn't have any more space in my room.

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:34.590
How on Earth can you drink that much...?

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:37.300
"Clean up your act!"

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:40.590
And so yeah...

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:43.390
I take it Makoto-san isn't a fan of alcohol?

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:47.810
Nah, it's not like that.
She still goes out with her friends and stuff.

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:51.600
My sweet little sister.
Makoto Kiriyama, a whole 21 years old!

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:53.190
A budding third year college student!

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:54.820
Member of the dance club!

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:56.400
Part timer at a café!

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.530
Wow, that's <i>so</i> Tokyo!

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:00.700
And the whole job search thing has her a bit nervous!

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:02.820
Yeah, I know how she must feel.

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:06.830
Makoto! Why must you shirk me so!

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:09.540
Makoto...

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:11.080
Hmm, that reminds me, though...
Makoto...

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:13.960
Well, Makoto-chan is not exactly fond of drunks.

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:18.510
If it's not alcohol she hates, but just drunk people...

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:21.220
You could always just try
drinking a bit less if you wanted-

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:23.850
Drink... less...?

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:26.560
Oh, my! Nao-san hold it together!

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:32.730
Is that Makoto-san?

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:36.230
She's buying drinks at the convenience store!

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:38.990
Hey, Makoto-san.

00:03:38.990 --> 00:03:40.820
Oh, back from work?

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.570
Planning on drinking a bit at home today?

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:43.530
Yes.

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:45.740
Care to join me?

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:49.370
Whoa-ho-ho! Do I ever! Do I ever!

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:51.500
Home at last.

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:56.000
<i>Yipee! I get to drink with Makoto-san tonight!</i>

00:03:57.880 --> 00:03:59.090
Now then!

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:00.050
Oh, my!

00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:02.630
That's the sound of the diamond-cut can there.

00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:04.010
"Diamond-cut"?

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:08.640
When you open it this diamond pattern
forms on the surface of the can.

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:12.270
Oh you're right. It's all bumpy...

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:16.230
Apparently that technique was originally created
to increase the strength of a given material.

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:20.530
And the name "Hyoketsu" itself means frozen,
which I guess makes things harder too, huh?

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:23.570
You know, you're a lot like Nao-san.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:25.280
Watch your mouth.

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:31.040
I've spent so long drinking with her and listening
to her explain it all so much, it just sort of stuck.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:34.000
Behold! The great bumpiness of Hyoketsu!

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:39.670
This here is based off of the Miura Fold,
a technology developed for space missions by NASA!

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:43.420
When they launch those rockets
they need things as light as possible.

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:47.680
So, the Miura Fold came about
to offer lightweight durability!

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:51.720
The can manufacturers want to cut costs
by using less aluminum,

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:54.100
but they can't cut back on durability.

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:58.810
So they apparently developed
this diamond-cut based on the Miura Fold.

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:00.900
A little fold can change everything.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.240
Wow!

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:03.820
Enough chit-chat, then.

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:05.070
Oh, right!

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:06.570
Cheers!

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:11.790
<i>A true sparkling diamond!</i>

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:15.790
That lemon packs a kick!

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:21.340
I was expecting it to be sweet, but it's much lighter
and tastes like an actual lemon, huh?

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:27.720
Chu-hi can tend to have really unnatural
sort of flavoring which can be a real downer.

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:30.890
But I like Hyoketsu because
it has that fresh juice sort of taste.

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:35.230
The grapefruit one also tastes like it was
freshly squeezed straight into the can...

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:40.360
<i>Would she hate me if I told her she looks
just like Nao-san when she drinks too...?</i>

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:45.610
So, hey, what's the workforce like?

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:46.610
Huh?

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:52.120
Are quotas rough and stuff?
Do people blame everything on millennials?

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:53.870
Whoa, where is all this coming from?!

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:57.040
I'll be on the hunt for work pretty soon.

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:59.830
I don't really know what it's like in one
of these companies and I'm worried...

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:02.420
Jeez, I'm sorry.

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:04.130
I'm probably a little drunk.

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:05.630
Let's just drop it.

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:09.840
W-w-well if there's anything
I can help with, feel free to ask away!

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:13.510
Are interviews nerve-racking?

00:06:13.510 --> 00:06:16.230
You bet! To the highest degree!

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:20.520
How do you present yourself?

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:24.480
With lots of motion! Like, you are
giving every bit of yourself to it!

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:28.780
Talk about how you love the company!
Admire it! Adore it! Let them really know!

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:31.530
Really? That sounds so embarrassing...

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:34.040
It is and this was too...!

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:38.910
I know! Just talk the way Nao-san does whenever
she's telling someone about some sort of drink.

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:40.040
What...?

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:44.800
I mean, she makes it seem so fun,
and so easy to understand doesn't she?

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:49.260
Why not try talking like that,
but about the company and about yourself?

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:52.800
W-well let's just give it a shot.

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:55.310
Think of this as practice!

00:06:56.810 --> 00:06:58.310
Well, then...

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:02.940
There is still one more thing to say about Hyoketsu...

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:04.940
Indeed, and that is...?

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:07.070
The straight juice!

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:10.070
It's the most important point in the fruitiness of Hyoketsu.

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:19.750
But Hyoketsu freezes

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:22.630
the freshly squeezed juice as-is and ships it.

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:26.340
The very name itself means "frozen"!

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:29.090
No heat treatment or water added then!

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:32.050
That's why it's "straight juice"!

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:35.350
It's always better to be straight
about something in the end!

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:37.010
You're in!

00:07:37.470 --> 00:07:39.480
See? That was good!

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:41.190
Y-you think so...?

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:43.310
I'm home...

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:44.730
Oh, that must be Nao-san.

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:47.150
No more overtime, pleeease!

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:49.860
I neeeeeeed a drink.

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:50.860
Hey...

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:51.610
Wait!

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:53.110
Are you two bonding over drinks?!

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:55.320
Why don't you join us Nao-san?

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:57.700
I'm not drinking today...

00:07:57.700 --> 00:07:58.370
What?!

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:02.040
I'm just gonna eat this
convenience store dinner and go to bed...

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:03.460
Are you, now...?

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:06.250
If you want to drink, just do it.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.630
You don't need to force yourself...

00:08:09.630 --> 00:08:10.920
Jeez! Which is it, then?!

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:12.590
Nao-san, please don't stand up while you eat!

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:14.720
What do you want from me?

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:17.140
I just don't like drunks.

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:18.600
How so, then?

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:21.770
Like when people get too close
and start acting too friendly.

00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:24.690
Ah, yeah. I know the type!

00:08:24.690 --> 00:08:28.900
And when people just get so loud
without a care for anyone around them.

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:32.240
Yup, yup! Definitely seen that before!

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:34.910
People who act exactly like you are right now!

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:36.530
But I'm sober as can be!

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:42.540
I knew you really just hated me!

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:44.710
I don't hate you...

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:47.290
I just think you should drink more like a normal human.

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:51.920
Keep drinking like that
and you're going to wear yourself out...

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:54.430
Hmm? Could you repeat that for me?

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:55.760
Just forget it...

00:08:56.430 --> 00:08:57.850
Come again?

00:08:57.850 --> 00:09:00.060
It's not... I just...

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:01.140
Makoto-san!

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:03.810
Be straight! Remember, just be straight with her!

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:07.440
<i>"It's always better to be straight in the end"!</i>

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:10.520
I'm...

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:12.570
I'm just worried about you!

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:15.070
You really shouldn't drink that much!

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:18.160
Wait, seriously?!

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:18.820
Drop it!

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:21.330
You were worried about me?!

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:22.290
Enough, already!

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:26.500
Jeez, you should have just said so in the first place!

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:28.630
I said drop it!

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:33.710
Well! With that out of the way,
I think I'll have a drink!

00:09:33.710 --> 00:09:35.130
Just one though.

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:35.720
Okay!

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:39.720
Well, I'm heading off to bed, then.

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:41.970
'Kay, see you tomorrow.

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:43.640
Goodnight.

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:47.190
<i>They've got the same necklaces!</i>

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:53.230
Go...   Good morning...

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:57.200
What about that whole talk we had yesterday?!

00:09:57.200 --> 00:10:00.950
Ah, well, it was so much fun, we just...

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:08.750
It ain't so bad if we just drink like this
from time to time, you know?

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:09.790
Nao-san!

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:13.300
Yeah, from time to time...

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:13.960
Wait, what?!

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:20.180
After a night of drinking frosty Hyoketsu,
no thin ice was left between the two sisters.

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:21.890
Don't you two need to get ready?

00:10:21.890 --> 00:10:23.180
Got the day off.

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:24.390
No classes for me today.

00:11:56.150 --> 00:12:02.240
There's also a whole other "Strong Series"
of Hyoketsu that is 9% alcohol.

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:09.620
Not only that, but there's the "Zero Series" that have
no sugar, no purine, and no added sweeteners.

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:12.750
That might be good to keep in mind,
if you want to drink healthier!

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:15.460
Here's to another night!
